## Interface: 16001
## Title: |cffC9A24ATwich|rUI Workshop
## Notes: Browse the recipes of your professions, queue crafts, see the combined materials still needed, and scan auction prices to see which crafts may be worth making. Loaded only when you open it (/tui workshop); keep it turned on alongside TwichUI.
## Author: twichie
## Version: 1.0.0
## RequiredDeps: !!!TwichUI
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\!!!TwichUI\media\icon
## X-License: MIT (code); see !!!TwichUI\LICENSE
## Category: Interface Enhancements

# Names, limits and small checks (no game calls, no frames); it creates R.Workshop
Data.lua
# The combined materials and what is still needed (pure)
Materials.lua
# The saved queue of the current character (TwichUIDB.workshop; this addon has no saved variables of its own)
Queue.lua
# What the profession window offers: the player's own recipes, their output and materials (game reads only)
Observe.lua
# Auction prices: the price service, what one craft costs and earns (saved in TwichUIDB.workshop.prices; no game calls, no frames)
Prices.lua
# The Opportunities list: rows, filter, sort, the basis text (pure)
Opportunities.lua
# The price scan of the open auction house (started only by the player's click)
Scan.lua
# What the window shows and does, without any frame
Session.lua
# The window (last: it tells TwichUI the addon is ready)
Window.lua
